#### **7.3 Tool Execution (Dispatch & Parallelization)**

**Location:** [agent/tool_executor.py](agent/tool_executor.py#L1)

**Sequential vs parallel:**
- Default: **parallel** (up to 8 workers) if tool calls don't overlap on file paths
- [_should_parallelize_tool_batch](agent/tool_dispatch_helpers.py): checks path overlap, destructiveness (`rm`, `git push`), start order (approvals must serialize)
- Destructive tools: terminal commands matching `rm|rm -rf|git push|git force-push` → sequential even if safe
- Image generation: max 4 concurrent (FAL rate limit)

**Result handling:**
- Tool result = string (JSON for structured tools, plain text for shell)
- Oversized results (>100KB): spilled to `~/.hermes/sessions/{session_id}/{tool_name}.output`
- Injected as `{"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_123", "content": "..."}`

