### **8. Prompt / System Message Strategy**

**Location:** [agent/system_prompt.py](agent/system_prompt.py#L1), [agent/prompt_builder.py](agent/prompt_builder.py#L1)

**Three-tier assembly (joined with `\n\n`):**

**Tier 1: Stable** (byte-stable for cache)
- Identity: [DEFAULT_AGENT_IDENTITY](agent/prompt_builder.py#L236)
  ```
  You are Hermes Agent, an intelligent AI assistant created by Nous Research. 
  You are helpful, knowledgeable, and direct...
  ```
- Tool guidance: "Here is how to use your tools: function calling via JSON schema..."
- Computer use guidance (if enabled)
- Subscription block (Nous Portal benefits)
- Tool-use enforcement (per-model: "Always call tools, never describe hypothetically")
- Environment hints (shell type, OS, Python version, working directory)
- Platform hints (CLI: "You are in an interactive terminal"; Telegram: "Messages limited to 4096 chars")
- Coding guidance: "When writing code, prefer clear variable names..."
- Hermes help reference: "For Hermes configuration/setup questions, see https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs"

**Tier 2: Context** (mutable but long-lived)
- Caller-supplied `system_message` kwarg
- Discovered context files (in order of resolution):
  - `.hermes.md` / `HERMES.md` (project-specific directives)
  - `AGENTS.md` (team-level, discovered in git root)
  - `.cursorrules` (Cursor IDE compatibility)
  - `SOUL.md` (user identity, replaces DEFAULT_AGENT_IDENTITY if present)
- Coding-workspace snapshot (project structure, dependencies, last N errors from CI)
- Threat scanning: injection patterns blocked; benign content scanned once

**Tier 3: Volatile** (rebuilt every turn)
- Skills index: available skill names + one-line descriptions
- Memory snapshot (if external memory provider enabled)
- USER.md profile (user preferences, recurring corrections)
- External memory provider block (e.g., Honcho dialectic context)
- Timestamp / session_id / model / provider line

