### **19. Data Flow Diagram (Textual)**

```
User Input (CLI, Telegram, Discord, etc.)
    ↓
[CLICommandsMixin | GatewayPlatformAdapter]
    ↓
AIAgent.run_conversation(user_text)
    ├─ [MemoryProvider.prefetch] → session search, external memory recall
    ├─ [ContextCompressor.should_compress] → decide if context > threshold
    │   └─ If yes: [ContextCompressor.compress_context] → call summary LLM
    ├─ [AIAgent._build_system_prompt] → assemble 3-tier prompt
    │   ├─ Load identity (SOUL.md or DEFAULT_AGENT_IDENTITY)
    │   ├─ Scan context files (.hermes.md, AGENTS.md, .cursorrules)
    │   ├─ Inject skills index
    │   └─ Inject memory snapshot
    ├─ [AIAgent._build_api_request] → chat completions payload
    │   ├─ Sanitize messages (surrogates, non-ASCII, tool IDs)
    │   ├─ Estimate tokens
    │   └─ Apply provider-specific headers
    ├─ [OpenAI SDK | Provider Adapter]
    │   └─ POST /v1/chat/completions (with streaming)
    │       ├─ Live streaming: delta → stream_delta_callback
    │       └─ On finish_reason="tool_calls": tool_calls array
    ├─ [AIAgent._execute_tool_calls_concurrent | sequential]
    │   ├─ Parallel? Check path overlap, destructiveness
    │   ├─ [model_tools.handle_function_call(name, args)]
    │   │   ├─ Dispatch via [tools/registry.dispatch]
    │   │   └─ Tool handler returns string (JSON or plain text)
    │   ├─ Tool guardrails: pre-call decision (ALLOW/DENY/CLARIFY)
    │   ├─ Collect results; if oversized, spillover to disk
    │   └─ Append as tool messages → messages list
    ├─ If finish_reason == "tool_calls": Loop back to API call
    ├─ Else (stop/length): Exit loop
    ├─ [AIAgent._ensure_db_session] → create SQLite row if needed
    ├─ [AIAgent._flush_messages_to_session_db] → persist transcript
    │   └─ Ephemeral scaffolds NOT persisted (pop markers)
    ├─ [MemoryProvider.sync_turn] → async memory write (if async)
    └─ Return final_response
        ↓
    [Render to User]
    ├─ CLI: print via prompt_toolkit or _safe_print
    ├─ Telegram: send_message (chunked to 4096 chars)
    ├─ Gateway: POST result to session DB / webhook
    └─ Desktop TUI: inject into chat feed, update UI
```

**Background (async, post-turn):**
```
[Background Review Thread]
    ├─ If complex task (5+ tool calls, fixed bug, new workflow)
    ├─ [Curator.review] → evaluate if skill should be saved
    ├─ [SkillManager.save_or_update_skill] → persist to ~/.hermes/skills/
    └─ Next turn, skill available in schema
```

